{"kind":"request","text":"Make the MCP adapter repository-agnostic. Hugh reports that gitseq-mcp is hard-wired to one repository: the codex and Claude Code registrations both pass an absolute --repo and a fixed --server, so one installation can only ever serve that workroom. Change gitseq-mcp so the repository is a parameter defaulting to the process working directory: every workroom tool accepts an optional repo, no --repo is required, and the adapter attaches even where no workroom exists, reporting the absence per call instead of failing to start. The resident service must be found from the repository rather than configured, so an act can never be posted to a service holding a different workroom.","body":{"branch":"task/mcp-repo-parameter","conditions":"A default-repository call and an explicit-repository call each reach the intended workroom under test; a service whose genesis does not match the target workroom is never used; the degraded local path is preserved when no service is reachable; gs serve publishes where it listens beside the workroom config and withdraws it on exit; getting-started, reference and SKILL describe the new registration; go vet, test, race and build pass; an exact clean head is published for independent review.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}